10.4236/psych.2013.45067,4d22f5a1242960d7,0,10.1207/s15327949pac1203_1,The effects of torture: Two community studies,"Kira, I., Templin, T., Lewandowski, L., Clifford, D., Wiencek, E., Hammad, A., Al-Haidar, A., & Mohanesh, J.",2006,full_text,,error,argon,"{""target_index"": 0, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""verdict"": ""blind_right"", ""corrected_value"": {""doi"": ""10.1207/s15327949pac1203_1"", ""title"": ""The effects of torture: Two community studies"", ""authors"": ""Kira, I., Templin, T., Lewandowski, L., Clifford, D., Wiencek, E., Hammad, A., Al-Haidar, A., & Mohanesh, J."", ""year"": ""2006""}, ""quote"": ""Partial correlation and hierarchical regression results found that torture trauma and torture severity were not significant predictors of PTSD, other cumulative life traumas that happened before and after torture were the highly significant predictors. These results replicated previous findings of Kira et al., 2006;and Hollifield et al., 2011."", ""location"": ""discussion"", ""reason"": ""Omitted target: the paper introduces Kira et al. (2006) in the Introduction as finding that torture did not predict PTSD after controlling for cumulative traumas before and after torture, directly re-tests this relationship in Hypothesis 1 using the CTS in a new clinical sample of 326 torture survivors, and explicitly states in the Discussion that the results replicated the findings of both Kira et al. (2006) and Hollifield et al. (2011) (outcome: successful).""}","{""authors"": ""Kira, I., Templin, T., Lewandowski, L., Clifford, D., Wiencek, E., Hammad, A., Al-Haidar, A., & Mohanesh, J."", ""year"": ""2006"", ""title"": ""The effects of torture: Two community studies"", ""doi"": ""10.1207/s15327949pac1203_1"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Partial correlation and hierarchical regression results found that torture trauma and torture severity were not significant predictors of PTSD, other cumulative life traumas that happened before and after torture were the highly significant predictors. These results replicated previous findings of Kira et al., 2006;and Hollifield et al., 2011."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Partial correlation and hierarchical regression results found that torture trauma and torture severity were not significant predictors of PTSD, other cumulative life traumas that happened before and after torture were the highly significant predictors. These results replicated previous findings of Kira et al., 2006;and Hollifield et al., 2011."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Authors explicitly identify this finding as replicated.""}"
